  "problem": "Arthur and Sara are finding the best recipe for chocolate muffins, and they test three different oven cooking modes, mode $1,$ mode $2,$ and mode $3.$ They also try two types of yeast, A and B.\n\n- They use mode $1$ to cook the $45%$ of their muffins, and $80%$ of those muffins turn out well.\n\n- They use mode $2$ to cook the $35%$ of their muffins.\n\n- They use mode $3$ to cook the $20%$ of their muffins, and $90%$ of those muffins turn out well.\n\nIf $65%$ of all muffins were prepared with yeast A, $82%$ of yeast A muffins turn out well, and $68%$ of good muffins were prepared with yeast A, what is the probability that a randomly chosen muffin cooked with mode $2$ turned out well? Round your answer to $3$ decimal places.",
  "worked_solution": "",
